WEBVTT

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.460
Manager!

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:11.260
The testing period is starting,
so could you decrease my shifts a little?

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.640
Yeah, sure.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.140
Come to think of it, are you feeling all right?

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.140
Oh...

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.350
HACK

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.060
<i>Love and peace!</i>

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.700
I was nervous you would quit after that.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.370
Oh, that wasn't bad enough to...

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.990
Knock it off, Kouno!

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.950
You can't work like that!

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.210
Even though I'm making delicious soup?

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.420
Welcome!

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.300
Table for one?

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.680
Right this way.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.480
Here, Yuuta.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:08.400
I'm so nice that I'm giving you
New Year's money just this once.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.240
Ready? I'm gonna drop it.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.490
It looks like you two are having fun.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.000
I'm tired so I'm going on break.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:28.670
Um... I wonder how much
it would take to make me quit.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:30.170
Then you do wanna quit?!

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.340
Higashida!

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:33.970
BAM

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:35.840
Help me study!

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.300
That can be your White Day return gift!

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.010
That's sudden and shameless!

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.110
LIFE ISN'T THAT EASY

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.520
But why do you need help?

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.280
My grades at school have been so lousy
that my mom said if I get

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.400
bad grades on the upcoming tests,
I have to quit working and go to cram school.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.240
But I can't help you.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:24.160
Why not?!
You'd be in trouble if I quit, right?

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.700
Yes, but...

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.700
You'd be fine if the manager quit,

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.500
but you couldn't hack it if I quit, right?!

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.000
Well... yeah, but...

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.340
Higashida?!

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.800
But I've got tests coming up, too...

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.760
So what? Don't be stingy!

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.800
Kisaki, if you would,
please tutor Miyakoshi.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:45.970
What?

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.810
Oh, is that a customer's...

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.730
This baby?

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.060
She's my daughter.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:53.940
Daughter?!

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.400
Kisaki, you have a child?!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.860
Yeah, well. Her name is "Hime."
Be nice to her.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.160
HIME KONDOU

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.370
N-Nice to meet you...

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.950
Why did you bring your baby here?

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:12.170
That's right, Kisaki. This is a workplace.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.630
You're the one who told me.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.630
<i>My kid won't eat cucumbers
unless I peel them.</i>

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:19.630
<i>Really?</i>

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.630
<i>What a pain!</i>

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:21.680
<i>Kids are so fussy.</i>

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.010
<i>Tell me about it!</i>

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.600
<i>They've been here a long time.</i>

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.100
<i>Since lunchtime, so what, four hours now?</i>

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:31.480
<i>Sometimes they bring their kids in here.</i>

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.270
<i>A family restaurant is a fine place
to have a long conversation,</i>

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.940
<i>but I hope their children are okay.</i>

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.820
<i>I'm sure someone's watching them.</i>

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.780
<i>Still, it makes me nervous
that they're not together.</i>

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.070
<i>That's what you think?</i>

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:47.080
<i>Yeah. I'd rather have them bring the kids...</i>

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.370
That's what you said, so I did.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.500
My mom's at home,
but she spoils this one rotten,

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.170
so is it okay if I keep bringing her in?

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.500
A-Actually...

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.670
Okay!

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:03.680
Manager?!

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.010
Kisaki, you...

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.010
Miyakoshi!

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.020
What is the value of a 45 degree tangent
for this ABC triangle?

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.020
Chemistry?

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.020
Physics, isn't it?

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:16.980
It's mathematics.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.820
That's math?!

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.230
It's definitely not chemistry.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:24.530
Hime...

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.030
She's right!

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.370
Come on, Miyakoshi.
She got it right, so pet her head.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.750
Just tutor me for crying out loud!

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.250
I'm your elder!

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.130
Sorry, but somebody who can't distinguish
between math and chemistry

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.510
is a little beyond me...

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.300
T-That was just one time!

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.430
Welcome!

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.230
Hello.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.860
What kind of dialect is that?!

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.070
It's English.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.280
Um, Kouki Saiki?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:06.240
University student, 20 years old.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.240
SAIKI KOUKI

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:14.040
He says his parents are Japanese,
but he was born and raised

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.170
in another country,
so he doesn't speak any Japanese at all.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:20.210
Apparently, a friend of his put in an
application for him without asking.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:24.210
I CAME, BUT I HOPE YOU TURN ME DOWN
 QUICKLY SO I CAN GO HOME...

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.050
Kisaki, you can speak English too, huh?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.180
Yeah, well...

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.180
PHEW

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:31.350
Then please say this to Mr. Saiki...

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:35.310
This restaurant is full of oddballs,
so he'll probably get a skewed view of Japan,

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:38.060
but these people are actually
extremely rare.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.690
Higashida...

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.650
So what are you gonna do?

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.450
And so, this is the newbie, Saiki.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.240
Hey!

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.960
He was nervous,
but seemed like a serious person,

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.920
so I thought maybe he'd work out...

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.420
Who's gonna train him?

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.590
Can't you speak English, Higashida?

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.670
I know the grammar,
but can't really hold a conversation...

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:09.050
I don't speak it at all.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:12.050
Just talk normally to him.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:13.560
That wouldn't work!

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.310
Even without English,

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.640
you can make yourself understood
with gestures and stuff.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:18.520
And the mood!

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.650
What do you mean by "gestures"?

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.940
Um... Waving your hands about?

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:25.690
You mean like punching him?
Knocking sense into him?

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:27.030
Yeah, more or less.

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.530
That's not it at all!

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.990
All right, Kisaki, you can train Saiki.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:37.250
Fine. I'll train Saiki to be the perfect gofer.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.630
Okay. I'll do my best to
learn English conversation.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:47.760
Since I'll be busy training Saiki,
you'll have to take care of Miyakoshi.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.340
You heard her!

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.350
Okay.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:58.100
Well, it is true that I'd be in a jam
if you quit, Miyakoshi.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.600
Higashida!

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:01.230
I'll go to your house for our first session.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.020
No way! My house is off limits!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:07.110
After all, I can't concentrate here.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:09.780
And my place is too far away
and I don't have study tools.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.860
You live near here, don't you, Higashida?

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.530
Forget it! It's dangerous!

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.490
For a girl to come to my house alone...

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.080
What if something happened to you?!

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.670
You would do something to me, Higashida?!

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.300
What's wrong, Big Bro?

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:35.050
Someone's coming over
after work tomorrow,

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.140
but you don't have to make
any kind of fuss about it.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:42.060
Oh my, Daisuke. You have a friend!

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:46.270
Oh, Mom! I figured even Daisuke
would have one friend.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:48.020
That's right, dear.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.110
You shouldn't be surprised that
Daisuke has one friend.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.360
So who is it?

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:55.820
A girl from work.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.870
Well done, Daisuke!

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.540
That's fantastic!

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.580
Not bad, Big Bro!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:06.540
All of the young ladies there
are cute and polite.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.670
Yeah. Yeah, that's right.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:13.680
Daisuke?!

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.560
So this is your house, Higashida!

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.610
Drop the wide-eyed
customer service act here. It's creepy.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.900
I-I'm not putting on an act.
We're not at work.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.070
And don't call me creepy.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.240
Welcome!

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:38.240
Welcome!

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.540
Wow! Big Bro, you really did
bring someone over!

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.460
Don't tell me you've been
lying in wait all this time?

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.210
Of course we have!

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:52.170
O-Oh my! Daisuke!
Hana is so surprised!

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:54.590
Miyakoshi...

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:56.510
Come on in.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.350
Sorry it's so cramped.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.850
Not at all. Thank you for having me over!

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.980
What would you like to drink?

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.640
Do you like sweets?

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.020
Um...

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.020
Never mind that!
This way, Miyakoshi...

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.400
I'll bring you a snack later on!

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:12.400
Make yourself at home!

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.530
Okay!

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.150
Miyakoshi...

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:19.160
Shut up. I am a guest in your house,

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.450
so how do you expect me
to act towards your family?

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:24.870
Relax. I'm not gonna put on any act
while you're teaching me.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.500
Are you sure? All right then...

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.040
PHEW

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.960
<i>This Miyakoshi puts me at ease?!</i>

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.460
So exactly what don't you understand?

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.090
I don't know what I don't understand.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.800
Then why don't we start with English?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:40.850
Okay.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:47.890
We should probably review basic adverbs
and the definition of nouns,

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.020
but this time, let's work on
the sentences here that use the infinitive

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.150
and rote memorization of the
predicates and vocabulary.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.780
So we'll focus on this teaching unit...

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.820
You know that was all in Japanese...

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.200
That was Japanese?!

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:06.910
I think I can get by in life
without knowing the "infinitive."

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Miyakoshi...

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.880
Right now you're having trouble
because you don't know it.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.010
I'm going to take over Mom's work,

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.590
so I don't even need
an academic background!

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.430
What does your mom do?

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:26.600
You don't know?
It's only local, but she's on TV.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.390
TV?

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.900
Youko Miyakoshi, the cooking expert.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:35.110
<i>Love and peace!</i>

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.360
Schoolwork is indispensable
when it comes to searching for

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.570
a line of work that truly suits you,

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.370
not one imposed upon you
because of heredity.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.030
H-H-Heredi...

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:45.870
Never mind. Pipe down and study!

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.250
So you're 20, too, huh, Saiki?

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.670
Yes... R-Right.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:57.300
Then let's celebrate that coincidence
by forming a 20-year-old alliance!

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:01.300
It'll be me, you, Adachi, Mura and Kisaki!

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.430
I'm still 19.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.100
Okay with me.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.640
As usual, I don't know
what you're going on about...

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.140
All right! Then I'm gonna quit today!

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.860
I'll have hamburg steak.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.740
Kouno! You're quitting all of a sudden?

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.530
Is there something going on at home?

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:22.990
Nope, not at all.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.240
Then why would you quit?!

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:29.000
It's interesting when the founder
of an alliance is the first to quit, isn't it?

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.000
Kouno!

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:34.130
CLICK CLICK CLICK CLICK

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.960
Come back, Kouno.

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:40.630
Think about it.

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:43.050
If the founder of the alliance
is the first to quit,

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:45.100
but then is the first one
to come back part-time...

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.060
It's interesting?!

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.350
Y-Yeah. So come back.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.560
I'll do it. I'll come back!

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:58.820
Dammit. Bad luck.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:02.450
I don't want you.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:04.360
Give us Hana or Shiho.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.570
We're fans.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.960
Sir! Please calm down...

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:17.130
Yes, I'm fine.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:20.670
You needn't be angry for my sake,
although I appreciate it.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:27.100
Excuse me. Please continue.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.430
Never mind.

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:33.390
That was a pain, huh, Mura?

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.730
Oh, Kouno. You came back.

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.650
Mura, this is the service industry
so as a woman,

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:40.730
you should learn how
to put on a cordial smile.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.490
Cut it out, Kouno!

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.650
Good point.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:47.160
Okay, Kouno, would you do something
that puts your life in danger?

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.780
I may be able to muster a smile then.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:52.410
Apologize, Kouno.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.000
I can smile if I want to,
but for some reason,

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.920
people around me have
a questionable reaction.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:02.010
Don't worry about it.
You're a hard worker, Muranushi.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.590
Really? Thank you, Adachi!

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:13.270
Adachi? What's wrong, Adachi?
Hey, Adachi!

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.270
<i>I guess that was a fail...</i>

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.190
Adachi!

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:18.650
You've got it rough, too.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.690
I want her to go back to the old Shiho.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:25.320
She wasn't always like that?

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:25.650
BAM

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.860
MONEY

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.030
Of course not!

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.700
A long time ago, she was quiet...

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.660
The first time I met her...

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.500
It was when my old man went
to Shiho's house to borrow money...

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:40.840
<i>I was told to wait in the garden,
but this is a forest.</i>

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.550
<i>Wh-Who are you?</i>

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.350
<i>Um...</i>

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:52.560
<i>Wanna eat some grass?</i>

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.100
<i>Grass?</i>

00:14:56.810 --> 00:15:00.230
<i>I see. So you live here.</i>

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:02.570
<i>I'm the son of the guy
who came over to borrow money.</i>

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:04.820
<i>I'm eating your grass.</i>

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:05.990
<i>Y-Yeah.</i>

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.820
<i>So why are you crying?</i>

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:12.830
<i>Nobody at kindergarten will be my friend,</i>

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:15.540
<i>just because they say I'm rich!</i>

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:20.290
<i>Mama died from a disease and
Papa is always busy with work.</i>

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.340
<i>Shiho is all alone!</i>

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:25.050
<i>There's a positive side to that.</i>

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:30.260
<i>Nothing good could ever come of
making friends with people who judge</i>

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:33.140
<i>others on whether they have
money or not, starting in kindergarten.</i>

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:36.220
<i>Th-That's too difficult for Shiho to understand.</i>

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:41.400
<i>Okay, the friend thing aside,
I'll bring it up with your papa casually.</i>

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:45.360
<i>B-But Papa is busy working
to make more money.</i>

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:52.450
<i>At this rate, your papa is gonna
have a major loss in the future.</i>

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:57.330
<i>He's gonna lose a precious fortune.
The bond with his daughter.</i>

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:58.830
<i>Y-Yeah.</i>

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:03.920
<i>Sheesh. Money causes nothing but trouble,
whether you have it or not.</i>

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.130
<i>Well, that's what I'm told, anyway.</i>

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:10.800
<i>At home, my mom always gripes
and shares her world view.</i>

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.600
<i>Shiho doesn't understand
difficult things like that.</i>

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:20.140
<i>Mister...</i>

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:23.730
<i>Your daughter seems lonely</i>

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:27.110
<i>because you don't pay much attention to her,</i>

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:29.110
<i>so please play with her more.</i>

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:31.610
<i>Thank you for the advice.</i>

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:35.330
<i>That wasn't casual at all.</i>

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.240
<i>Oh well, I am a kid.</i>

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:38.580
<i>Thanks for the grass.</i>

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.340
DAYS LATER...

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.250
GRUMBLE RUMBLE

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:48.340
<i>I pretty much cleaned out all the
edible grass around here.</i>

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:49.880
<i>Y-Yuuta!</i>

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.050
<i>Huh? Shiho.</i>

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:52.300
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:53.550
<i>Although you do live nearby...</i>

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.350
<i>Shiho wanted to thank you, Yuuta.</i>

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:59.680
<i>Ever since then, Papa's played
with Shiho every day!</i>

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.350
<i>That's good to hear.</i>

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:04.730
<i>And he assigned me men in black
to make sure nobody bullies me.</i>

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.980
<i>So you're giving up
on making friends, huh?</i>

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.490
SEVERAL DAYS LATER...

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:17.830
<i>Papa says that your family
owes him a lot of money, Yuuta.</i>

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:19.490
<i>That's what I hear.</i>

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:24.580
<i>If you and I get married,
that debt could be wiped out.</i>

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.040
<i>No thanks.</i>

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:31.630
<i>Crap!</i>

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.300
I've always regretted that moment.

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:37.550
If I had been a little more mature...

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.510
If I'd let her down more gently...

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:40.890
So you did refuse then.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.060
After all...

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.350
It's been a long time,
but why don't you apologize?

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:49.070
You might even see if
you can take back dumping her.

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:51.110
Take back?

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:53.530
A-are you telling me to marry her?!

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:55.740
I wouldn't go that that far...

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:58.530
but it might be to your benefit
to give her a positive sign.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:00.950
Th-That's fraud!

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.000
You are a male host.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.370
Deceiving one or two women
comes with the territory.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.170
Shiho!

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:12.420
There's no way you're getting an
extension on this month's payment.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:14.920
No, th-that's not it.

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:18.010
Um... Uh... Please m... ma...

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:18.720
Ma?

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.890
Mar... mar... mar...

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:22.890
Why does this guy come up blank
unless it has something to do with marriage?

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:23.890
Mar...

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:28.900
Mark me up as much as you like.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.780
No, not when you request it.

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:38.660
It's hopeless!
I can't understand any of this!

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.660
Okay, only one thing to do...

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:45.330
Let's try to guess what's on the exams,
so you can memorize only that stuff.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:47.370
That's a lot!

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.500
Um, maybe this?

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:50.130
Yeah!

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:52.210
Also, here, here and here...

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:53.210
Y-Yeah...

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:54.880
Maybe this and this, too.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.220
Here too, I think.

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:58.300
That's almost everything!

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:01.260
Life isn't that easy, you know.

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.680
I apologize for the intrusion.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:05.680
It was no bother at all!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:09.480
Higashida, that jerk.
He gave me homework!

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:11.480
I'll get revenge on him someday!

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:16.490
Hello there! Might you be the
Miyakoshi my son has mentioned?

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:18.450
Higashida's father...

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.990
Thank you for letting me come over today!

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:28.120
Daisuke! I've lost respect for you!

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.380
Oh, shut up!

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.800
Now that the testing period is over,

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:36.970
please put me back on my usual shifts.

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:38.470
I hope you did well on the tests.

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.010
So you're back to the normal schedule?

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:44.890
Now I can finally stop working.

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:48.060
That won't do, Kisaki.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:50.810
Training Saiki has worn me out.

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:53.310
Has Saiki gotten used to the work?

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:56.530
Yeah. He's learned a little Japanese, too.

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:57.940
Say something, Saiki.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:01.950
Where can I buy cigarettes and diapers?

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:03.070
Kisaki...

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.370
He's getting better, right?

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:05.410
Higashida!

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:06.950
Kouno...

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:09.500
It's Adachi! He's so dazed from
what happened the other day

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.000
that he won't even snap at me!

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:14.710
If nobody snaps at me, there's no point
in doing anything stupid!

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.710
Higashida, please snap at me!

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:18.880
I can't do that.

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:20.380
Wh-Why not?!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:21.840
That's not my jurisdiction.

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:22.840
Jurisdiction?!

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:26.810
Adachi...

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:28.930
Higashida...

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.600
Has something happened?

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.940
N-No, nothing special...

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:36.520
But Kouno is crying.
He says you've been acting weird.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:37.900
Sob...

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:40.610
I-I've just been thinking about something...

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:46.990
I can't focus on my work these days...

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.120
It is important to be engrossed in something,

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.460
but that should coexist with
what else you need to do.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.500
Coexist?

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.500
With snapping at Kouno.

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:55.500
Snapping at him?!

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:00.760
Higashida!

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:01.630
I did it!

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:02.630
What is it?

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.640
Listen to this!
Mom says I don't have to quit!

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.680
Then your grades...

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:08.680
No, not that!

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:13.980
Hana! Eat your breakfast and go to school!

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:15.690
You've got tests today, don't you?

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:17.860
Hana!

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:22.740
New York, California, Los Angeles,
Las Vegas, Washington, Texas...

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:28.450
I slept through the tests,
so that was a disaster,

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.790
but Mom said I can keep working!

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.040
What was all of my hard work for?

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.710
All right!

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:37.500
I'm gonna work hard today, too!

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:12.510
She's so cute.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:14.930
My granddaughter is adorable.

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:16.980
I love playing dress-up with her!

00:23:17.020 --> 00:23:17.600
SQUEEZE

00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:20.730
Hime, thank you for being born!

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:23.690
And thank you for being born too, Ki!

00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:25.990
You're welcome.

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:36.000
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.740
Next time, it'll be summer!

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:29.240
In Hokkaido, winter vacation is long,

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:30.410
but summer vacation is short, right?

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:32.200
Yes! It was so dissatisfying
back in elementary school!

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:33.830
It's because summer itself
is short in Hokkaido.

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:36.000
YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE I CAN ASK

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:36.000
Next time,
"You're the Only One I Can Ask!"
